<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Batten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Batten is a small peninsula on the eastern side of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plymouth-sound">Plymouth Sound</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/devon">Devon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Excavations have shown it was a trading port in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, linking south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> with Brittany and the Atlantic coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> through the exchange of metals and other goods. In the 20th century it was the site of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-air-force">Royal Air Force</a> flying-boat station.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-batten.jpg" alt="Mount Batten" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trysca · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mountbattenpeninsula.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
